00],[17.3,17.58,16.63,17.2,1060800]],"about":{"what":"VirnetX Holding Corp (VHC). This chart runs from Jun 10, 2010 to Oct 15, 2010.","setup":"The stock rose about 80% in the three months before the base. It then formed a base for about 5 weeks, peaking at $6.69 and pulling back 16% at its deepest. Daily price ranges tightened on the right side of the base.","outcome":"On Aug 27, 2010 it closed at $7.32, its first close above the base high of $6.69. Volume that day was 1.9M shares, 4.01x the prior 10-day average of 461K. It held, never closing below the level three days running, reached a best close of $18.55, and the chart ends at $17.20.","lesson":"This is an example of a textbook breakout: a base, then a close above it on heavy volume, and it held. This is the pattern the rules are built around."}}